    f.render_widget(Paragraph::new(line), r);
    // Set cursor position for terminal? ratatui Frame has set_cursor_position? In 0.30, f.set_cursor_position((x,y))? Actually Frame::set_cursor_position takes (u16,u16)? Let's set cursor to input position (for tmux cursor? But capture-pane doesn't show cursor, so not critical. Still, set for correctness.
    // Cursor x = inner.x + 1 (leading space) + cursor_char_idx (clamped to visible)? y = inner.y
    // Compute cursor char idx from byte idx (search_cursor is byte idx in input String). For ASCII, same. For UTF-8, need char count up to byte idx.
    let cursor_byte = app.search_cursor.min(input.len());
    // Ensure byte idx is char boundary (it should be, since we move by chars). Compute char idx.
    let cursor_char_idx = input[..cursor_byte].chars().count();
    // If input truncated/scrolled, adjust? For now, assume no scroll, cursor within visible.
